# Experiment visual evidence

## Why

Physical control behavior (pointing, shutters, capture timing, attitude) is visible across time in **videos and plots**, not in aggregate CSV/JSON alone. Reward curves are fine for quick estimates; **deeper behavioral claims require visual artifacts**.

## Hard evidence (required)

For ML experiments, hypothesis cycles, and pipeline Phases **2–4**:

1. **Export videos and reward plots** from training runs when behavior is in scope (`TrainingWorkflowConfig` defaults: `train_episode_videos=3`, `eval_episode_videos=2`; `export_episode_reward_plots=true` in experiment `profile.json`). Phase 2 `--screen` / `--full` must pass **`--export-artifacts`** when those flags are enabled — do **not** rely on default trim. Trim only when the user explicitly passes **`--trim-artifacts`** (see learnings.md `phase2-export-artifacts-not-trim-default`).
2. **[`video-frame-inspect`](../skills/video-frame-inspect/SKILL.md)** — extract PNGs from `.mp4`; read frames with vision; cite `manifest.json` path in Phase **2.3** / **4.3**.
3. **[`visual-output-verification`](../skills/visual-output-verification/SKILL.md)** — agent pre-check on concrete artifacts before behavioral verdict language.
4. **User sign-off** — agent frame review is pre-check only; user confirms before Phase 4 close ([`minimal-feature-review`](../skills/minimal-feature-review/SKILL.md)).

Pair with [`isolated-notebook-hypotheses`](../skills/isolated-notebook-hypotheses/SKILL.md) **evidence-first**: persist real examples (frame findings, plot paths, manifest paths) — not only aggregate KPIs or run logs.

## Evidence tiers

| Tier | Use for |
|------|---------|
| **KPI JSON / CSV** | Quick reward trends, wall time, smoke pass/fail |
| **Plots** (`returns_by_episode`, episode reward/torque grids) | Episode-level diagnostics; cite paths |
| **Video + frame manifest** | Pointing, shutters, capture quality, learning behavior over time |
| **User-watched MP4** | Final behavioral judgment before closeout |

## Forbidden

- Closing Phase 2–4 on KPI JSON or `run_log.md` alone when videos or plots were exported or are needed for the claim.
- Running Phase 2 with default artifact trim when `profile.json` enables plot/video export — operators expect sibling-experiment artifacts under `results/artifacts/`; KPI JSON alone is not enough.
- Verdict language about shutters, pointing, or “learned behavior” without `video-frame-inspect` findings (or explicit user frame review).
- Saying “videos exist” without **full paths** and manifest path.
- Discussing pipeline run results in chat (review, recap, arm comparison) with **KPI-only** tables and no MP4 paths when videos were exported.
- Marking a visual/render task done from code inspection only.
- Committing the full experiment dump as semester-report evidence — curate into `docs/report/semester-project/figures/` with section tags ([`generate-research-report`](../skills/generate-research-report/SKILL.md) figure freeze; learnings.md `report-figure-curate-not-dump`).
- Declaring semester-report PDF layout OK from `.tex` alone — use `/review-research-report` checklist **I** (render pages + vision; learnings.md `report-layout-visual-pdf-review`).
- Wiring report figure panels without vision-checking each panel against the caption’s intended process, or using parallel phase names vs Methods (learnings.md `report-figure-caption-process-match`).
- Shipping byte-identical `fig_*.png` under different names, or loss-diagnostic plots as “learning curves” instead of `returns_by_episode` (learnings.md `report-figure-artifact-integrity`).

## Platform note

Slow MP4 export ([D-013](../../docs/research/DECISIONS.md)) is **performance debt**, not permission to skip behavioral evidence. Document export mode in Phase 2.3; improve encode path separately — do not treat missing video as an acceptable experiment outcome when behavior was the question.

